>
  <p>Katrina Ridout is an Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD) who focuses on fertility, pregnancy and postpartum nutrition. As an APD, Kat can assist anyone wanting to improve their health, providing education, strategies and motivation for concerns such as diabetes, cardiovascular disease, weight management, disordered eating, gut and metabolic conditions, food allergy and intolerance, and general healthy eating. Her main area of interest is prenatal nutrition.</p>

  <h2>Who Kat sees</h2>
  <p>Women and couples planning a pregnancy, going through fertility treatment or IVF, during pregnancy (including gestational diabetes), and after birth. Kat also works with general nutrition clients.</p>

  <h2>How to refer</h2>
  <p>Email the referral, with any relevant pathology or clinic letters, to <a href="mailto:info@katridout.com.au">info@katridout.com.au</a>, or use the <a href="/contact-us/">contact form</a>. You can also simply ask your patient to book a free 15-minute call with Kat at katridout.com.au. No referral is required for a patient to book.</p>

  <h2>Medicare</h2>
  <p>Eligible patients with a GP Chronic Condition Management Plan (GPCCMP) may be able to claim a Medicare rebate on dietetic consultations. Patients pay the consultation fee and receive a receipt to claim with Medicare.</p>

  <h2>Telehealth and in person</h2>
  <p>Kat consults by telehealth anywhere in Australia, and in person at Milton Village Medical, Level 1, 36 Baroona Road, Milton QLD 4064.</p>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <h3>Who is Katrina Ridout?</h3>
  <p>Katrina Ridout is an Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD) with Dietitians Australia who focuses on fertility, pregnancy and postpartum nutrition. Read more <a href="/about-kat/">about Kat</a>.</p>
  <h3>What conditions do you see?</h3>
  <p>Preconception and fertility nutrition including IVF preparation, PCOS, endometriosis, pregnancy nutrition, gestational diabetes, pregnancy weight, postpartum recovery and breastfeeding, and general nutrition.</p>
  <h3>Do you see patients outside Brisbane?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Kat consults by telehealth anywhere in Australia.</p>
</Article>
